Rules:
Batchcode is always unique (no need to match by itemcode); all batched belong to a catalogue entry. Catalogue is the presented one to the consumer, batch is each individual batch.
AccountId is always unique (no need to match by category).
I am creating a new Eto.Forms.Panel. It will be shown when a user selects a thing from the left side. I want you to write a panel that serializes and deserializes the following to native JSON types into a form. The DTO is usually the same as the database object. Do not use NumericUpDown or NumericStepper. Use only textboxes, checkboxes or buttons, datetimepickers for normal fields and GridView for lists. You will see if something is a list, it will be mentioned either in the type or explicitly. Re-check your output for syntactic validity and for logic sanity.

The program should never crash, so write a ValidateInputs() function that returns (bool IsValid, string ConsolidatedErrorList) and check against it whenever serialize is called. The theme definition:
