We do basically everything through the API. We have both a desktop and a web software, web software is basically a bunch of static html files with cshtml/razor path mapping. This is so because it should be easier, not harder, to write a browser that can run this, and this should run WELL on nascent browsers and runtimes. As it currently stands, all the above code work well and fast on Servo (browser) project and considering Ladybird is likely ahead, would likely run well on that too.


